    <sectiondef kind="define">
      <memberdef kind="define" id="global_8hpp_1a68447123f2c27bb7bcdbbaec4091dab7" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>CRITICALMESSAGE</name>
        <initializer>std::string critical_error = fmt::format(&quot;Failure: {} : {} : {} : {}&quot;, \
                                         e.what(),                     \
                                         __func__,                     \
                                         __FILE__,                     \
                                         __LINE__);                    \
<ref refid="classMessage_1aa085f3b7f644c7c1075eac59e3c2f7a9" kindref="member">Message::CriticalMessage</ref>(critical_error);</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Logs the active exception together with function, file and line. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Expands to several statements that build <computeroutput>critical_error</computeroutput> via fmt and pass it to <ref refid="classMessage_1aa085f3b7f644c7c1075eac59e3c2f7a9" kindref="member">Message::CriticalMessage</ref>. <simplesect kind="pre"><para>Must be expanded inside a catch handler with an exception variable named <computeroutput>e</computeroutput> in scope, and with fmt and <ref refid="classMessage" kindref="compound">Message</ref> available. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Declares a local variable named <computeroutput>critical_error</computeroutput>; avoid using the macro where that name is already taken. It expands to more than one statement, so guard it with braces when used as a single statement. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
