        <detaileddescription>
<para>First expands CRITICALMESSAGE, then invokes <computeroutput>callback</computeroutput> with the status from statusForException. For a busy database (503) the exception&apos;s own message is returned so the client knows to retry; for any other failure (500) the detailed <computeroutput>critical_error</computeroutput> string is returned and the raw exception text is kept out of the response. <simplesect kind="pre"><para>Requires <computeroutput>e</computeroutput>, a callable <computeroutput>callback</computeroutput> compatible with CALLBACK_, and the names used by CRITICALMESSAGE to be in scope. </para>
</simplesect>
